 there's also  a way to completely change your starting  zone to do this talk to the person on  the beach and complete that initial  quest but do not start the next one  instead open your map and you'll notice  that the next quest is available on all  four beaches now all you have to do is  make the long journey to the beach you  want and then kick off the opening  quests in that territory instead  questing is new world's core activity  and in the game there are four types of  quests that can be completed main side  faction missions and town projects  completing any of these rewards you with  experience points to level up and doing  so earns you an attribute point but  before we talk about the attribute  points let's talk about the most  efficient ways to earn more xp in less  time first off don't ignore the side  quests as tempting as it may be to try  to focus solely on the main stuff it's  smart to pick up the available side  quests along the way this will save you  so much time and you can earn more xp  for example  old me used to do all of the main  missions until they were too high of a  level for me so then i would go over to  the side quest to try to reach that  level oftentimes going back to the same  areas that i just was in for the main  quest so be better than old me grab  those side quests and tackle them while  you're already out completing other  things in the world i can't stress  enough how much travel time you'll save  and while you're already grouping side  and main quests make sure to toss in  some town projects and faction missions  town projects can typically be found in  the town hall and be on the lookout for  very simple projects that can be  completed without going out of your way  too much for example i stumbled on two  listings for hunt boar at the same time  this became an easy killing two birds  with one stone type of situation as now  i was completing two projects with  similar requirements at the same time  while just casually traveling to a quest  and even though town projects are good  to do whenever faction missions should  be a top priority when they are the  first three of your day these daily  bonuses can be seen in the upper left  hand corner of the faction mission  select screen and it should say three of  three if you haven't done any yet  according to the developers this bonus  nets you about 200 percent more xp than  the mission was originally worth  so let's recap really quick grouping  your quest together are key for more  experience in cutting down travel time  main side and town projects are perfect  for grouping together all the time but  your faction missions will get the most  benefit when they're the first three  that you're doing that day all right got  it got it let's hydrate  let's jump back in let's do it  to save even more on travel time you'll  want to make sure you're checked in at  the end of the area you're questing at  this way after you've done a handful of  quests you can just teleport back to  town turn those in and get right back  out into the world to complete some new  ones however keep in mind that the  cooldown for recalling to the end is 60  minutes don't want to wait walk or pay  for fast travel well there's also dying  on purpose in respawning at the nearest  camp or settlement it'll just cost you a  little bit of weapon durability  settlements are also a great place to be  when you're done playing new world  logging out while in a town can earn you  a rested xp bonus when you return to the  game that means that any task that gives  you level xp will grant you a little  more as long as the bonus is active and  now you don't have to feel bad when you  go out and live your real life because  when you return you're getting a little  bit extra towards your progression  another way to level up quickly comes in  the form of territory standing with each  rise in an area's reputation comes a  large amount of xp for your character  you increase territory standing using  all your normal experience gaining  activities like questing crafting  killing mobs etc completing a quest in  everfall earns experience forever fall  crafting something in first light earns  xp for first light and every new  standing level comes with a reward one  of which can be xp buffs so if reaching  max level is your top priority then i'd  advise paying attention to your standing  and picking the xp or standing buffs  when available some extra leveling tips  include picking up notes around the  world and adding them to your journal  these are only worth around 100  experience but if you're out killing a  mob and a note is right in front of you  on a crate it wouldn't hurt to pick it  up plus you get the added bonus of being  able to read it later and get more  insight on new worlds lore  and speaking of killing mobs keep in  mind you only need two light attacks in  order to gain experience of someone  else's kill so if you can manage to  squeeze those in while you're passing  someone fighting then boom you've got a  tiny bit of xp without much effort and  we'll discuss a little more about pvp  later in the video but since we're  talking about experience flagging  yourself for pvp is another great way to  earn extra because of its five percent  bonus  now finally let's go back and talk about  what you're going to do with all of that  experience and leveling up spending  attribute points new world does not  feature a traditional class system like  other games in its genre instead the  characters attributes heavily impact  your play style the attributes available  at launch include strength dexterity  intelligence focus and constitution  strength will affect your melee weapon  damage while dexterity does a little bit  of the same but also improves the  effectiveness of ranged weapons  intelligence can boost the power of  magic weapons while focus affects the  recovery rate of mana as well as your  healing output and that leaves  constitution which improves 