e a handful of  attack types there's slash thrust strike  as well as fire and ice just to name a  few and each of those has a different  effect on the different enemy types so  here's how the colors break down orange  means critical damage white means normal  damage yellow means that enemy is weak  to that damage type and blue means that  that enemy is resistant to it for  example the corrupted are weak to thrust  damage but resistant to ice  meanwhile the lost are resistant to  thrust and weak to ice it's sort of like  the pokemon type charts if you're  familiar with that already and similar  to swapping different pokemon in and out  of the battle to gain the advantage new  worlds classless system means players  aren't tied to a specific damage type  and can switch to anything on the fly  getting all blue numbers from slash  switch to thrust still getting blue  numbers whip out that elemental damage  weapon and try that out instead points  gained through this weapon mastery  system can be used in each of the two  skill trees there are 38 total abilities  per weapon type but mastery has a level  cap of 20. so at this time it is not  possible to unlock every ability  available however it's still really good  to experiment with every weapon early on  to figure out what suits you but try to  settle on your favorite two by the time  your character is about to hit level 20.  this way you can focus on gaining  mastery in those two  higher weapon mastery means better  weapon skills which in turn could mean  the upper hand in combat leading to more  experience especially in pvp when it  comes to armor there are some important  things you need to know about weight for  starters you can mix and match different  weights to your heart's content you  don't have to stick to one style the  combined heaviness of those chosen  pieces are what determine what weight  class you're in and thus affects your  movement and damage output like  characters have a rolling dodge and a 20  damage bonus medium characters have a  quick hop instead of a roll and also  have a 10 damage buff and a 10 longer  crowd control heavy characters get  knocked down to a slow side step but  have 15 percent increase block and 20  percent longer crowd control and a  really good tip to remember with your  gear early on is to salvage  everything you may be tempted to toss  what you don't want in storage or put it  up for sale at the trading post but  trust me  storing it is a waste of time and it's  very unlikely that someone's gonna buy  it because they just receive that same  reward from the exact same quest so  salvaging can free up your inventory and  give you repair parts to help with your  favorite weapons dwindling durability  crafting is essential in new world and  you'll be doing everything from creating  and modifying weapons and armor to  cooking food in order to keep your  character alive but your crafting is  nothing without other skills like  gathering unless you plan on buying all  of your resources and if so make sure  you're buying from a settlement that's  close to those resources because the  price will be less also keep in mind  that each town has some free resources  scattered around so make sure you grab  those if you spot them in the game there  are 17 trade skills split up into three  categories and your level in the 10  gathering and refining skills have major  effects on the seven crafting skills  higher gathering gives you the ability  to detect special resources on your  compass while higher refining skills  makes you more efficient with resources  so leveling each of these different  areas is definitely worth it and all 17  skills have a max level of 200 so  there's plenty of room for you to grow  however i would suggest specializing in  one of the crafting skills at a time  leveling multiple refining and gathering  skills can be fairly simple but due to  the resource pool becoming smaller each  time you craft it can be a little  difficult to level like weapon smithing  and armoring at the same time and if  you're planning on doing a lot of  gathering as you should i'd suggest  investing in some quality tools first  upgraded tools can make the gathering  process much faster as well as increase  your chances of gaining things like  extra azoll  so there you have it all of the useful  tips to help you hit the ground running  in new world if you have any tips of  your own please hit the comment section  and share with the whole class and if  you found this video helpful at all hit  the like button if you didn't also go  down to the comments and let us know  what questions you still have about new  world so we can possibly cover them in  the next video thanks for watching  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

